## Hybrid Materials
polyMOFs: A Class of Interconvertible Polymer-Metal-Organic-Framework Hybrid Materials
A bottom-up strategy is used to generate porosity from non-porous, one-dimensional, amorphous polymeric materials by their transformation into crystalline polyMOF materials. These materials har
ness the advantages of the porosity and crystallinity of MOFs along with certain attributes of the polymers, such as facile film formation and greater chemical stability.
